Claude"},{"repo_name":"MatterHackers/agg-sharp","commit_timestamp":"2026-09-29T23:53:49Z","branch":"main","commit_sha":"946abde1f6b0cc434facb4d6e1c2ea12be0b45c5","github_link":"https://github.com/MatterHackers/agg-sharp/commit/946abde1f6b0cc434facb4d6e1c2ea12be0b45c5","commit_subject":"SvgWidget now draws with the full agg/Svg renderer (SvgDocument.Parse + SvgRenderer.RenderToImage) instead of SvgTools.SvgParser, so fill/stroke opacity, caps, joins and presentation attributes inherited from a group render as they do for StaticData icons since e0f37bd8. Sizing is unchanged: the document is rendered at its own size times Scale and copied top-left into the width*Scale by height*Scale box, cropped rather than stretched. A negative width or height (the markdown remote-image caller passes none) now takes the document's size instead of allocating a -1 sized buffer. The renderer reads strict XML, so a malformed SVG throws from LoadSvg; its only caller besides tests, ImageLinkAdvancedX, already catches and logs that. SvgWidgetRenderTests covers fill-opacity, group-inherited stroke with fill none, and the scale/anchor sizing.","ai_tool":"Claude"},{"repo_name":"ProjectSidewalk/SidewalkWebpage","commit_timestamp":"2026-09-29T23:53:44Z","branch":"develop","commit_sha":"c6a57842d39d1e8e635d77fa700d2f80c1522fdb","github_link":"https://github.com/ProjectSidewalk/SidewalkWebpage/commit/c6a57842d39d1e8e635d77fa700d2f80c1522fdb","commit_subject":"Have Claude Code sign GitHub posts with its model and effort level (#5592)","ai_tool":"Claude"},{"repo_name":"microsoft/vscode","commit_timestamp":"2026-09-29T23:53:37Z","branch":"main","commit_sha":"bd991c73fbc9ed98bd416696e1e3b4c746e2c1d8","github_link":"https://github.com/microsoft/vscode/commit/bd991c73fbc9ed98bd416696e1e3b4c746e2c1d8","commit_subject":"agentHost: Keep remote hosts alive while agents are running (#338392)","ai_tool":"Copilot"},{"repo_name":"buildkite/buildkite-mcp-server","commit_timestamp":"2026-09-29T23:53:27Z","branch"